{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795284781,"nonce":"J7Eqc3JySsB6RLYKlwqYi5oz1JA=","message":"Landed in commit 0072bd9 (the frames of the bus), commit 3e52b94 (the messages and the match of one machine), commit 9f82b45 (the timeline), and commit 826bf22 (the session with the lobby). Tests run up to three machines over a bus in memory: every machine counts the same kills in the same order over two minutes, a hit takes effect only on the machine that flies the target, the next member flies the bots on when the host leaves, and a remote plane never steps backward when states arrive in bunches, after a stall of the sender, or on a slower route.\n\n**Ruling: the messages use Postcard.** Why: a published wire format with derived code replaces a hand-written codec. Cost: a state takes about 60 bytes, and design.md says 40.\n\n**Ruling: the owner of a plane sends its score in each state.** Why: a player that comes later then sees the right scores. The kills also arrive as events, in one order for all.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}